    "Habitat is common Singapore (e.g.,vertical greenery, streetscape, urban park/garden, community farm, commercial farm, golf course, turf, skyrise greenery).\n(>30%). \nHabitats which support <300 species, are asumed to be least priority for biodiversity and therefore automatically fall under this category e.g. farms.\nDistinct transitional habitats that comprise spontaneous vegetation, such as Scrubland/Grassland, are also considered low despite the habitat's uncommon frequency in Singapore. This habitat type acts as a transitional precurser to forest habitats which produce climax communities and as such are unlikely to remain in perpetual stasis as a natural habitat. Exposure or disturbance to land will enable this habitat to establish, and is therefore unlikely to ever be at risk due to rarity.",
